Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:26:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] sched: QoS parallelism on a virtual machine with only
 performance cores

With every vCPU in the performance cluster, sched_amp_qos_max_parallelism
reserved no capacity for background and utility work (its width came from
the empty efficiency cluster), so libdispatch never widened those queues
and opendirectoryd and the login path starved. A machine without
efficiency cores uses the cluster it has for every QoS class.
---
 osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c b/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c
index ba68df4..f88b423 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c
@@ -476,6 +476,14 @@ sched_amp_qos_max_parallelism(int qos, uint64_t options)
 	uint32_t ecluster_count = ecount ? 1 : 0;
 	uint32_t pcluster_count = pcount ? 1 : 0;
 
+	/* A homogeneous virtual machine may expose only performance cores.
+	 * There is no efficiency-only capacity to reserve for background or
+	 * utility work; those QoS classes use the available cluster as well.
+	 */
+	if (ecount == 0) {
+		return (options & QOS_PARALLELISM_CLUSTER_SHARED_RESOURCE) ? pcluster_count : pcount;
+	}
+
 	if (options & QOS_PARALLELISM_REALTIME) {
 		/* For realtime threads on AMP, we would want them
 		 * to limit the width to just the P-cores since we
